<section class="sg-sec" id="inspired"><h2>What it inspired</h2><ul class="sg-chain"><li><span class="sg-chain-n">Fischia il vento (Felice Cascione)</span> <span class="sg-chain-y">1943–1945</span><span class="sg-chain-h">new Italian words to the same melody (partisan song)</span></li><li><span class="sg-chain-n">The Hymn of EAM (Vassilis Rotas; recorded by Thanos Mikroutsikos, sung by Maria Dimitriadi)</span> <span class="sg-chain-y">1946–1949</span><span class="sg-chain-h">new Greek words to the same melody</span></li><li><span class="sg-chain-n">Primavera (Spanish Blue Division)</span><span class="sg-chain-h">new words to the same melody</span></li><li><span class="sg-chain-n">Vertu til er vorið kallar á þig (Tryggvi Þorsteinsson)</span><span class="sg-chain-h">new Icelandic words to the same melody</span></li><li><span class="sg-chain-n">A Soldier's Prayer (The Human Condition trilogy)</span> <span class="sg-chain-y">1961</span><span class="sg-chain-h">quoted in (heard briefly in the film)</span></li></ul></section>
